      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-09-28 04:07:21",
      "type": "原文",
      "type_label": "原文",
      "text": "A decade of launches from the edge of the world 🚀🇳🇿\n\nTen years ago, Launch Complex 1 was officially opened and became the world's first private orbital launch site.\n\nWhat seemed like a crazy idea - making dedicated launches to space frequent and affordable from a farm paddock in New Zealand - is now routine. Across Electron's history, LC-1 has been the launch location for commercial smallsats and science missions, national security payloads, and even a mission to the Moon. \n\nTwo launch pads and almost 100 launches later, LC-1 has made New Zealand one of the world's busiest launch countries - proving big things can happen in the most unexpected locations.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "",
      "engagement": {
        "bookmarks": 2,
